    "description": "Involved in a variety of projects, primarily in the area of Systems Management. \n- Team lead addressing security issues and enhancements for IBM Pureflex.\n- Work on Virtualization support for VMWare and Hyper-V in IBM VMControl. Advocate to the    \n     product owners for new features supporting these hypervisors. Write several components for the   \n     existing product. \n- Design and implementation of RDM, a deployment tool, including database design, and the design \n     and implementation of several subsystems. Technical lead for one release of the product. \n- Developed IBM Systems Management Asssistant from prototype through release 2.0. (Tool to \n     migrate settings and applications between machines running Microsoft Oses.).\nSmaller (single year) projects:\n- Level 3 support (highest level of customer support) – work with Level 1 and 2 support, and with \n     the customer, to debug problems. Make fixes in shipped products for customer problems as \n     required.\n- Part of a small team creating an add-in to Microsoft's SMS, allowing it to import and manage \n     updates to IBM hardware. \n- Win95 device driver to simulate a mouse on a handheld device.\n- Work on the VB runtime for Windows CE.\n- Port BMC (embedded controller ) software for new IBM Server hardware.",
